1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucrezia_di_Lorenzo_de%27_Medici
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucrezia de' Medici (4 August 1470 - between 10 and November 15 1553) was the eldest daughter of Lorenzo de' Medici and Clarice Orsini and mother of Maria Salviati and Giovanni Salviati, who was a cardinal from 1517 until his deat
2 CONC h. Her portrait was considered (as a newborn) as the baby Jesus in Our Lady of the Magnificat of Sandro Botticelli
2 CONT
2 CONT  Life, Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT She married on the 10 September 1489 to Jacopo Salviati.  By Salviati, she had 10 children, some of who were of great importance for the history of Renaissance Europe:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Cardinal Giovanni Salviati (Florence, 1490 - Ravenna, 1553)
2 CONT
2 CONT #Lorenzo Salviati (Florence, 1492 - Ferrara, 1539), senator and patron
2 CONT
2 CONT #Piero Salviati, patrician
2 CONT
2 CONT #Elena Salviati (Florence, 1495 circa - Genoa, 1552), married the Marquis Pallavicino Pallavicino and second marriage to the Prince Iacopo V Appiani in Appiano
2 CONT
2 CONT #Baptist Salviati (1498 - 1524)
2 CONT
2 CONT #Maria Salviati (1499 - 1543), married to Giovanni dalle Bande Nere. This marriage united the main branch and Popolano branch of the Medici family. His son, Cosimo, was named to lead Florence after the death of Duke Alessandro de'
2 CONC  Medici
2 CONT
2 CONT #Luisa Salviati, married Sigismund de Luna and Peralta
2 CONT
2 CONT #Francesca Salviati, married first to Piero Gualterotti and second, in 1533, to Ottaviano de' Medici and was the mother of Pope Leo XI
2 CONT
2 CONT #Bernardo Salviati (Florence, 1505/1508 - Rome, 1568) knight of the Order of St. John of Jerusalem; served Catherine de' Medici in France; 1561 Cardinal
2 CONT
2 CONT #Alamanno (1510 - 1571), patrician
2 CONT
2 CONT  Later Life
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacopo died in 1533, Lucrezia outlived him by twenty years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucrezia was a proud great grandmother to ten great grandchildren, through her daughter Maria, who would look after all of them. However, Lucrezia never really got to see them and tragically Maria died in 1543, aged 44. Lucrezia w
2 CONC as very upset by the loss of her daughter and she herself died 10 years later. Lucrezia's exact death date is unknown but it is known that she died between 10th and 15 November 1553.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her age at the time of her death was 83 years old, which was very old for women in the 16th century and she had outlived three great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Through her daughter Maria, Lucrezia is an ancestor of the Medici family as well as its descendants, an ancestor of the Kings of France and also the Kings of England. Her grandson was Cosimo I de' Medici, who became Grand Duke of 
2 CONC Tuscany, his son was Francesco I de' Medici who succeeded his father in 1574. Francesco had two daughters, both who married into important families and changed the course of history.
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco's daughters were Eleonora de' Medici and Marie de' Medici. Eleonora married Vincenzo I Gonzaga, their son was Francesco IV Gonzaga and through Eleonora, Lucrezia is an ancestor of the Dukes of Mantua and also of the Hous
2 CONC e of Habsburg-Lorraine. Through Marie, Lucrezia is ancestor of Kings of France, through Marie's marriage to Henri IV of France. Marie's grandson was Louis XIV of France. Louis's grandson, Philip, Duke of Anjou, became king of Spai
2 CONC n and is a direct ancestor of Juan Carlos, current king of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie also had a daughter called Henrietta Maria who married Charles I of England. Henrietta Maria and Charles were the parents of Charles II of England and James II of England. James was the father of Mary II of England, Anne of 
2 CONC Great Britain and James Francis Edward Stuart-'the Old pretender'. Charles, on the other hand, is an ancestor of Diana, Princess of Wales, and Sarah, Duchess of York. The 'Old Pretender' had two sons, Henry Benedict Stuart and Bon
2 CONC nie Prince Charlie-'the Young Pretender'. Henry Benedict was a cardinal, who died childless, while the 'Young Pretender' had an illegitimate daughter, Charlotte, Duchess of Albany. The claimant, through Charlotte, to this branch o
2 CONC f the House of Stuart is Peter Pininski.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrietta Maria also had a daughter, Henrietta 'Minette' Anne Stuart, who married Philippe I, Duke of Orleans and had issue. Her descent ultimately culminated in Franz, Duke of Bavaria, who is the current Heir General of the House
2 CONC  of Stuart and embodies the still continuing Jacobite claim to the thrones of England, Scotland, Ireland and France
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
