1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fran%C3%A7ois_III_de_Rye
2 CONT
2 CONT http://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=fr&u=http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_de_Rye&ei=jN3RT4mtAoak8gS5waXXAw&sa=X&oi=translate&ct=result&resnum=3&sqi=2&ved=0CFYQ7gEwAg&prev=/search%3Fq%3DPhilibert%2Bde%2BRye%26hl%3D
2 CONC en%26biw%3D1600%26bih%3D805%26prmd%3Dimvnso
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis de Rye is a French ecclesiastic of the seventeenth century. He was coadjutor archbishop of Besancon and titular Archbishop of Caesarea in Cappadocia from 1623 to 1636 , before succeeding his uncle Ferdinand of Rye as archb
2 CONC ishop of Besancon in 1636 until 1637 , the year he died. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis is the son of Rye Rye Philibert, artillery general in the Spanish Netherlands and Claudine de Tournon, sister of Cardinal François de Tournon . His first ecclesiastical benefice was the prior of Dampierre . After studying 
2 CONC in Rome , he was sent to Brussels at the court of the Archdukes Albert and Isabella , then sovereign of the Spanish Netherlands . It was rapidly appreciated the royal couple who appointed him chief of his personal chapel and Grand
2 CONC  Chaplain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT With the support of his uncle , he was climbing at the same time the level in the church by becoming diocesan canon of the metropolitan chapter and the 12 June 1599 Top dean of this chapter. In 1618 Ferdinand de Rye in the propose
2 CONC d chapter to be his coadjutor which was agreed on 16 October 1618 . A delay in the sending of the decision in Rome and the death of Pope Paul V carried back to his appointment effective 9 January 1623 . He was consecrated bishop i
2 CONC n 1626 while residing at Brussels . He succeeded his uncle on 20 August 1636 but never took his seat as he died eight months later in Brussels on 17 April 1637 , the day set for the delivery of the pallium . 
