2 CONT
2 CONT =Ippolito de' Medici=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Noble family Medici  
2 CONT * Father '''Giuliano de' Medici'''  
2 CONT * Mother '''Pacifica Brandano'''  
2 CONT * Born 1511''Florence?'', Republic of Florence  
2 CONT * Died 10 August 1535 (aged 24) Itri, Kingdom of Naples 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ippolito de' Medici''' (1511 – August 10, 1535) was the illegitimate only son of '''Giuliano di Lorenzo de' Medici'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ippolito was born in ''Urbino?''. His father died when he was only five (1516), and was subsequently raised by his uncle Pope Leo X and his cousin Giulio.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Giulio de' Medici was elected pope as Clement VII, Ippolito ruled Florence on his behalf. After the siege of Florence (1529–1530), however, Clement favored his other illegitimate nephew Alessandro, and made Ippolito first arc
2 CONC hbishop of Avignon and then cardinal instead (1529), sending him as Papal legate to Hungary, where he evidenced a talent for soldiering.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a friend to, and possibly had a liaison with Giulia Gonzaga, the Countess of Fondi.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1535 he acted as Florentine ambassador to emperor Charles V. Ippolito died from malaria in Itri, in southern Lazio, although there were rumours that he had been poisoned by Alexander, whose abuses he was going to denounce.
