1 NOTE 76 year old Bernabo of Milan, trusting and confidant, met his nephew Gian Galeazzo in May 1385 to discuss family matters.  Bernabo was seized by his nephew, and made his prisoner.  Gian then took over the city of Milan.  Bernabo's
2 CONC  palace was acked and burned by Gian's mob. Bernabo died in December 1385, supposedly poisoned by his nephew, the ursurper.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernabo Visconti, age 76, was buried with ceremony in Milan, an equestrian statue which he had designed,  was erected as he had planned.
1 NOTE Also Lord of Cremona, Lodi, Bologna
1 NOTE Ruler of Milan.  The family herald is of serpant or dragon devouring a man.
