1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleonora_Gonzaga,_Duchess_of_Urbino
2 CONT
2 CONT https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleonora_Gonzaga_della_Rovere
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonora Gonzaga della Rovere (Mantua, 31 December 1493 – Urbino, 13 February 1550) was the daughter of Francesco II Gonzaga, Marquis of Mantua and Isabella d'Este, daughter of Ercole I d'Este, Duke of Ferrara.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquisate of Mantua
2 CONT Gonzaga
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Gianfrancesco
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT Ludovico
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT Frederick I
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT Francis II
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT Frederick II
2 CONT Sons
2 CONT V · D · M
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT She was married to Francesco Maria I della Rovere (1490-1538), Duke of Urbino. The marriage by proxy took place in 1505, the nuptials four years later in Mantua[1]. Eleonora therefore arrived at the della Rovere court in Urbino in
2 CONC  1509[2].
2 CONT
2 CONT He ordered the expansion of the Imperial Villa in Monte San Bartolo, entrusting the work to the architect Girolamo Genga. The work was completed in 1540. The villa was a meeting place for countless artists and intellectuals[3].
2 CONT
2 CONT On the death of his uncle Julius II della Rovere pope in 1513, Francis returned to Pesaro, where he moved his court and family. In 1516, however, the new Pope Leo X expropriated him of all his domains. Eleonora and her family ther
2 CONC efore had to take refuge in Mantua; they returned to Urbino only after the death of the pope in 1521[2]. With the death of Leo X, Francesco also regained Gradara, given to him years earlier by his uncle Julius II, whose government
2 CONC  he entrusted to Eleonora[4].
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1538, on the death of his father, Guidobaldo II entrusted Eleonora Monterado and Mondolfo to his mother[5].
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage
2 CONT The couple had thirteen children[6][7][2][8]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Federico della Rovere (Urbino, 21 March 1511[9] - Urbino, 1511), died at two months;
2 CONT Guidobaldo II della Rovere (Urbino, 2 April 1514 - Pesaro, 28 September 1574), who married Giulia Varano and then Vittoria Farnese;
2 CONT Ippolita della Rovere (Urbino, c.1515 - Naples July 1538), who married Antonio d'Aragona, Duke of Montalto;
2 CONT Giovanna (Urbino, 1515 - Urbino, 1518);
2 CONT Giovanni (Urbino, 1516 - Urbino, 1518);
2 CONT Caterina (Urbino, 1518 - Urbino, 1520);
2 CONT Beatrice (Urbino, 1521 - Urbino, 1522);
2 CONT Francesco Maria (Urbino, 1523 - Urbino, 1525);
2 CONT Maria (Urbino, 1527 - Urbino, 1528);
2 CONT Elisabetta Isabella della Rovere (Urbino, 1529 - Massa, 6 June 1561), married Alberico I Cybo-Malaspina;
2 CONT Giulia della Rovere (Casteldurante, 1531 - Ferrara, 4 April 1563), who married Alfonso d'Este, Marquis of Montecchio;
2 CONT Giulio della Rovere (Mantua, 15 April 1533 - Fossombrone, 3 September 1578), cardinal.
2 CONT Violante (Urbino, 1535 - Urbino, 1538).
2 CONT
