1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rinaldo II Trinci (Foligno, ... - Milan, about 1452) was an illegitimate Italian Catholic bishop.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Corrado III Trinci, last lord of Foligno.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was in 1398 canon of the cathedral of Foligno and from the 1400 prior of the same. In 1437 his father forced him to be elected by the clergy bishop of Foligno. Pope Eugene IV, who had elected Cristoforo Corfini Boscari [2] to t
2 CONC he death of Giacomo Berti (Elmi), never wanted to recognize the bishop Trinci, who however remained at the head of the diocese until 8 September 1439, when, besieged Foligno da part of Giovanni Vitelleschi, he escaped to Ferrara. 
2 CONC [3] He then moved to Milan, a guest of the Sforza family, where he probably died in 1452.
