1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filippo_di_Piero_Strozzi
2 CONT
2 CONT Filippo di Piero Strozzi (French: Philippe Strozzi) (1541 – July 27, 1582) was an Italian condottiero, a member of the Florentine family of the Strozzi. He fought mainly for France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Florence to Piero Strozzi and Laudomia de' Medici. His father had been exiled from his native city, and had been received in France by Queen Catherine de' Medici, being appointed as Marshal of France. Filippo became
2 CONC  page of the future king Francis II.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1557 Strozzi entered the French army. Starting from first battles in Piedmont, he fought in numerous of the battles of the 16th century. In 1558 the took part to the siege of Calais against England, in which his father was kill
2 CONC ed. In 1560 he was sent to Scotland to fight for the rebels, and was made lord of Épernay. Three years later he became colonel of the Royal Guards.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1564 he came on help to Emperor Maximilian II during the Ottoman invasion in Hungary, and the following year he faced again the Ottomans at the siege of Malta. From there he moved to Rome, called to counter the Turk menace in t
2 CONC he Adriatic Sea, distinguishing himself in the defence of Ancona. He later fought also in Transilvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Returned to France in 1567, he fought against the Huguenots. Two years later he became the sole Colonel General (commander-in-chief of the army) of France, and subsequently took part to the long siege of La Rochelle. He was accomp
2 CONC anied by his friend Pierre de Bourdeille. In 1573 foughts alongside the House of Orange against the Spaniards.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1581 Filippo Strozzi exchanged the position of General Commander for that of lord of Bressuire and was called by António, Prior of Crato (Portuguese claimant to the Portuguese throne against Spanish Habsburg King Philip II) as 
2 CONC a private mercenary. With a contingent of French, Dutch, English and Portuguese volunteers, he set sail to the Azores, a Portuguese Atlantic territory that still did not recognize Philip II as king. His fleet was however destroyed
2 CONC  in the Battle of Terceira [also called Battle of Ponta Delgada, Battle of São Miguel] (July 26, 1582) by the Spanish navy under the great admiral, Álvaro de Bazán, 1st Marquis of Santa Cruz.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Ponta_Delgada
2 CONT
2 CONT Taken prisoner, he was executed at the age of 42, by being wounded to death and then thrown into the sea from a Spanish ship, as a pirate. The harsh punishments meted out to the unfortunate Strozzi and captured members of his crew
2 CONC s were carried out at the instructions of the Spanish admiral, despite much protest from his own crews.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Voir [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippe_Strozzi '''Wikipedia...''']
