0 @N6000000002322286017@ NOTE Giovanni became Pope Leo X. From 1513-1521, years considered to be the apogee
1 CONT of the Medici age, has been called "the century of Leo X". Leo X surrounded
1 CONT himself by 5 nephews and cousins whom he named cardinals, but he ruled less
1 CONT over Christianity than over arts and letters in the style of his father,
1 CONT Lorenzo the Magnificient, too occupied with the patronage to pay attention to
1 CONT an unimportant monk by the name of Martin Luther.
